<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="771548a">&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        EY involvement in development of&amp;nbsp;training varies from one project to the next and the role (i.e., client
        advisor vs. system integrator)&amp;nbsp;EY plays on the project is a major factor
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        In general terms, development of training content and material should focus on providing context for participants
        to&amp;nbsp;understand why a new platform, solution or system is being used
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        The EY role on the engagement will determine the involvement in developing the training material, but generally
        this should focus on contextualising the training so participants understand why they are doing things differently,
        using a new system etc.
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Where procedures have been updated, the basis for the training should be those updated procedures.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    In many cases, training content may be developed off shore or third party vendor. It is critical to check the training
    material not just for accuracy and quality, but also to assess adherence to the training design principles set in
    earlier phases.&lt;br /&gt;
    &lt;br /&gt;
    In addition, training content must be reviewed not only for basics, such as the screenshots matching the new system,
    but also to ensure that the integrity of the training content is maintained and complete. This means that training
    content addresses both system and process elements.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="3e7093c0"></attribute>
<attribute name="usageGuidance" nodeId="8e7c0d54"></attribute>
<attribute name="refinedDescription" nodeId="5c530ed2">&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Develop training material, including: 
        &lt;ul&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                participant guides,
            &lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                job aids,
            &lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                quick reference material,
            &lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                e-learning,
            &lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                instructor guides,
            &lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                case studies, and
            &lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                pre-reading material.
            &lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;/ul&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Design and develop the training feedback and assessment mechanisms to be used in order to evaluate the
        effectiveness of the training courses.
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
</Element>
